From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 4 AVPs from ETSI-TS183.059-1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ETSI-TS183.059-1 V2.1.1 defines these AVPs in vendor 13019, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  CNGCF-Address (600): Grouped, 2 members, clause 7.3.5
  SIP-Outbound-Proxy (601): OctetString, clause 7.3
  TFTP-Server (602): UTF8String, clause 7.3
  ACS-Server (603): UTF8String, clause 7.3

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
index a48da2b..67e40b8 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
@@ -346,4 +346,19 @@
 	<avp name="ETSI-Digest-Response-Auth" code="521" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="no">
 		<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
 	</avp>
+	<avp name="CNGCF-Address" code="600" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<grouped>
+			<gavp name="TFTP-Server"/>
+			<gavp name="ACS-Server"/>
+		</grouped>
+	</avp>
+	<avp name="SIP-Outbound-Proxy" code="601" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<type type-name="OctetString"/>
+	</avp>
+	<avp name="TFTP-Server" code="602" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+	</avp>
+	<avp name="ACS-Server" code="603" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="ETSI">
+		<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+	</avp>
 </application>
